1
00:00:58,100 --> 00:01:03,100
"Kiss Or Kill"

2
00:01:03,500 --> 00:01:06,000
(Episode 3)

3
00:01:22,680 --> 00:01:23,680
A-yang.

4
00:01:24,439 --> 00:01:25,680
Or should I say...

5
00:01:28,239 --> 00:01:29,239
Lin Yan.

6
00:01:31,799 --> 00:01:32,959
Lin Yan.

7
00:01:35,200 --> 00:01:36,719
Finally figured out your real name.

8
00:01:37,879 --> 00:01:40,480
I still go by Nie Chuan.

9
00:01:42,319 --> 00:01:43,599
Nie Chuan the mercenary.

10
00:01:43,920 --> 00:01:45,318
Or Nie Chuan the guide?

11
00:01:45,319 --> 00:01:45,920
Both.

12
00:01:46,079 --> 00:01:47,319
I'm an open book.

13
00:01:47,480 --> 00:01:48,879
Unlike some people.

14
00:01:50,319 --> 00:01:51,359
So hypocritical.

15
00:02:06,319 --> 00:02:08,400
Got it, Second Uncle. Understood.

16
00:02:23,240 --> 00:02:24,560
I'll be right there.

17
00:02:31,159 --> 00:02:32,280
You've got eyes on you.

18
00:02:35,599 --> 00:02:36,599
I'm warning you.

19
00:02:36,919 --> 00:02:38,280
You'd better behave.

20
00:02:38,439 --> 00:02:39,840
Your every move

21
00:02:40,159 --> 00:02:41,559
is under my watch.

22
00:02:41,560 --> 00:02:42,560
What could I possibly do?

23
00:02:43,159 --> 00:02:44,960
I just want to make some money with you.

24
00:02:45,599 --> 00:02:48,360
After all, we have some history,

25
00:02:48,879 --> 00:02:49,879
don't we?

26
00:02:54,240 --> 00:02:55,639
Then behave yourself.

27
00:02:56,039 --> 00:02:57,280
I'll be watching you.

28
00:03:48,759 --> 00:03:49,960
Relax.

29
00:03:51,120 --> 00:03:53,359
Who hasn't made a few mistakes

30
00:03:53,360 --> 00:03:54,879
in their youth?

31
00:04:02,400 --> 00:04:04,039
Please give me one more chance.

32
00:04:04,520 --> 00:04:05,918
You're still young.

33
00:04:05,919 --> 00:04:07,280
What happened this time

34
00:04:07,639 --> 00:04:09,120
isn't entirely your fault.

35
00:04:10,639 --> 00:04:11,639
You may go.

36
00:04:13,039 --> 00:04:15,319
Thank you, Second Uncle. Thank you.

37
00:04:36,120 --> 00:04:37,198
How could Father

38
00:04:37,199 --> 00:04:38,759
tolerate any flaws left behind?

39
00:04:39,439 --> 00:04:40,439
Good night.

40
00:04:42,000 --> 00:04:43,000
Clean it up.

41
00:04:43,079 --> 00:04:44,079
Yes, sir.

42
00:04:45,000 --> 00:04:46,039
I heard

43
00:04:46,040 --> 00:04:48,879
you brought that guide home.

44
00:04:50,160 --> 00:04:51,160
Yes.

45
00:04:51,879 --> 00:04:52,920
Yes?

46
00:04:55,040 --> 00:04:56,239
He's mine.

47
00:04:56,240 --> 00:04:57,240
Your methods

48
00:04:57,360 --> 00:04:58,438
won't solve the problem.

49
00:04:58,439 --> 00:04:59,599
What can't be solved?

50
00:04:59,600 --> 00:05:01,279
I have plenty of ways to make him talk.

51
00:05:02,120 --> 00:05:03,359
You lack patience.

52
00:05:03,360 --> 00:05:05,119
The Black Moon Society
won't give you patience.

53
00:05:05,120 --> 00:05:07,136
They're in a hurry for a
route to move their goods.

54
00:05:07,160 --> 00:05:08,160
Second Uncle,

55
00:05:08,360 --> 00:05:10,399
he's already agreed to provide the route.

56
00:05:10,639 --> 00:05:11,920
But he has one condition.

57
00:05:14,120 --> 00:05:15,000
Let's hear it.

58
00:05:15,001 --> 00:05:16,240
He wants to stay with us.

59
00:05:16,720 --> 00:05:17,839
Stay with us?

60
00:05:19,360 --> 00:05:21,240
Every segment of his route

61
00:05:21,519 --> 00:05:22,839
has to be cleared by him.

62
00:05:24,519 --> 00:05:26,198
Keeping him under our watch

63
00:05:26,199 --> 00:05:27,199
ensures the route is secure.

64
00:05:27,200 --> 00:05:29,399
Besides, we've got a lot going on lately.

65
00:05:29,759 --> 00:05:31,120
I need the manpower.

66
00:05:32,199 --> 00:05:33,519
A-yan,

67
00:05:33,800 --> 00:05:35,920
you know the rules of the game.

68
00:05:36,480 --> 00:05:38,240
If you bring someone in,

69
00:05:38,560 --> 00:05:40,680
whether he's good or bad,

70
00:05:41,480 --> 00:05:43,040
you vouch for him.

71
00:05:43,199 --> 00:05:44,199
Understood, Second Uncle.

72
00:05:44,720 --> 00:05:45,519
I'll take the responsibility.

73
00:05:45,520 --> 00:05:46,680
Can you handle it?

74
00:05:47,160 --> 00:05:49,160
Use the right person, and
they're your right hand.

75
00:05:49,399 --> 00:05:51,456
Use the wrong one, and
they're a knife in your back.

76
00:05:51,480 --> 00:05:52,800
I trust my judgment.

77
00:05:53,079 --> 00:05:55,399
Alright. You may go.

78
00:05:56,560 --> 00:05:58,080
I'll take my leave then, Second Uncle.

79
00:06:15,720 --> 00:06:16,758
You're really something.

80
00:06:16,759 --> 00:06:18,198
You take the guy and the route,

81
00:06:18,199 --> 00:06:19,696
and show off in front of Second Uncle.

82
00:06:19,720 --> 00:06:20,999
Aren't you going to leave anything for me?

83
00:06:21,000 --> 00:06:22,000
I have my plans.

84
00:06:22,319 --> 00:06:23,519
It's all for the company.

85
00:06:23,560 --> 00:06:25,119
Cut the crap.

86
00:06:25,120 --> 00:06:26,239
You're always preaching about the company

87
00:06:26,240 --> 00:06:27,040
and Second Uncle.

88
00:06:27,120 --> 00:06:28,120
You think I don't know
what you're really scheming?

89
00:06:29,000 --> 00:06:29,839
Let me tell you,

90
00:06:29,840 --> 00:06:31,958
don't think just because you're Second
Uncle's nephew you can take over.

91
00:06:31,959 --> 00:06:33,919
I've done so much
dirty work for Lin.

92
00:06:33,920 --> 00:06:34,639
It's way more than you

93
00:06:34,640 --> 00:06:35,999
just pointing fingers in the office.

94
00:06:36,000 --> 00:06:37,719
This is what it is today

95
00:06:37,720 --> 00:06:38,720
because of me.

96
00:06:38,759 --> 00:06:39,759
Are you done?

97
00:06:39,879 --> 00:06:40,879
Am I wrong?

98
00:06:42,360 --> 00:06:43,559
Just you wait.

99
00:06:43,560 --> 00:06:45,360
Sooner or later, I'll catch you slipping.

100
00:06:45,959 --> 00:06:46,959
Brother Scorpion,

101
00:06:47,399 --> 00:06:48,720
Father wants you inside.

102
00:06:54,759 --> 00:06:55,560
Brother Yan,

103
00:06:55,561 --> 00:06:57,319
you haven't played with me in so long.

104
00:07:01,160 --> 00:07:02,879
Can I come over to your place tomorrow?

105
00:07:03,040 --> 00:07:03,560
Father just

106
00:07:03,561 --> 00:07:05,000
rewarded me with a new toy.

107
00:07:05,040 --> 00:07:06,160
I'll bring it to show you.

108
00:07:08,079 --> 00:07:09,480
I'll be busy for a while.

109
00:07:09,759 --> 00:07:10,839
Once I'm done,

110
00:07:11,000 --> 00:07:12,120
I'll play with you, okay?

111
00:07:12,319 --> 00:07:13,360
Okay, Brother Yan.

112
00:07:14,199 --> 00:07:15,199
A-ren,

113
00:07:15,720 --> 00:07:16,839
remember what I told you?

114
00:07:17,360 --> 00:07:18,560
Those toys are too noisy.

115
00:07:18,959 --> 00:07:20,319
Don't play with them for too long.

116
00:07:21,319 --> 00:07:22,319
Got it.

117
00:07:22,360 --> 00:07:23,120
Brother Yan,

118
00:07:23,121 --> 00:07:24,801
remember to come find me when you're done!

119
00:07:51,040 --> 00:07:52,160
You were never

120
00:07:52,360 --> 00:07:54,000
this annoying before.

121
00:08:37,759 --> 00:08:38,759
So much good booze.

122
00:08:40,120 --> 00:08:41,638
If I had known three years ago

123
00:08:41,639 --> 00:08:42,720
you were worth this much,

124
00:08:43,440 --> 00:08:46,279
I would've stolen more than just a ring.

125
00:08:50,000 --> 00:08:51,000
What about you?

126
00:08:51,200 --> 00:08:52,559
A freelance mercenary

127
00:08:54,440 --> 00:08:56,080
coming here to muddy my waters?

128
00:08:57,519 --> 00:08:58,720
Life is tough.

129
00:09:00,440 --> 00:09:01,679
It's a long story.

130
00:09:06,639 --> 00:09:07,639
Have a drink.

131
00:09:11,200 --> 00:09:13,120
I don't like people using my things.

132
00:09:17,799 --> 00:09:18,840
So stingy.

133
00:09:20,200 --> 00:09:21,200
Am I wrong?

134
00:09:23,480 --> 00:09:24,480
Fine.

135
00:09:25,519 --> 00:09:26,600
Not just stingy,

136
00:09:27,120 --> 00:09:28,759
but also ungrateful.

137
00:10:03,240 --> 00:10:04,240
Is it good?

138
00:10:04,840 --> 00:10:05,840
It's great.

139
00:10:06,600 --> 00:10:08,039
Shame I can't enjoy it properly.

140
00:10:22,039 --> 00:10:23,039
Be a good boy,

141
00:10:24,360 --> 00:10:25,480
and you'll get your booze.

142
00:10:26,679 --> 00:10:28,200
As long as there's a deal to be made,

143
00:10:29,360 --> 00:10:31,039
I can be very obedient.

144
00:11:14,559 --> 00:11:15,559
These past few years,

145
00:11:16,440 --> 00:11:17,639
what have you been up to?

146
00:11:18,720 --> 00:11:19,720
Doing business.

147
00:11:20,159 --> 00:11:21,278
Doing business?

148
00:11:21,279 --> 00:11:22,879
Then I'm here to talk business with you.

149
00:11:23,120 --> 00:11:24,840
Why so eager to turn away a guest,

150
00:11:25,559 --> 00:11:26,559
President Lin?

151
00:11:27,039 --> 00:11:28,039
And you?

152
00:11:28,960 --> 00:11:30,519
After you left,

153
00:11:31,120 --> 00:11:32,120
where did you go?

154
00:11:33,759 --> 00:11:34,960
I went to a lot of places.

155
00:11:36,433 --> 00:11:41,313
Up north, down south, to the mountains,

156
00:11:42,519 --> 00:11:43,639
and by the sea.

157
00:11:44,519 --> 00:11:45,320
Running from what?

158
00:11:45,440 --> 00:11:46,440
On the run.

159
00:11:47,840 --> 00:11:49,200
And while I was at it,

160
00:11:51,120 --> 00:11:52,120
looking for you.

161
00:11:57,200 --> 00:11:58,759
Don't drink all by yourself.

162
00:12:07,720 --> 00:12:09,320
Sometimes I wondered

163
00:12:10,639 --> 00:12:12,759
what it would be like to see you again.

164
00:12:15,960 --> 00:12:17,279
Now that I have,

165
00:12:18,266 --> 00:12:19,305
is it completely different...

166
00:12:19,360 --> 00:12:20,360
Totally different.

167
00:12:26,200 --> 00:12:27,960
I imagined many ways we'd meet again.

168
00:12:28,440 --> 00:12:29,960
Maybe on some battlefield,

169
00:12:30,960 --> 00:12:32,639
you'd smile at me.

170
00:12:33,200 --> 00:12:34,240
Maybe.

171
00:12:35,466 --> 00:12:36,986
Maybe I'd save you one more time.

172
00:12:38,919 --> 00:12:40,440
The only thing I didn't expect

173
00:12:41,519 --> 00:12:43,320
was you pointing a gun at me.

174
00:12:51,440 --> 00:12:52,440
Lin Yan,

175
00:12:53,519 --> 00:12:54,759
in these past three years,

176
00:12:55,519 --> 00:12:57,039
did you ever think of me?

177
00:13:05,120 --> 00:13:06,200
You talk too much.

178
00:13:11,759 --> 00:13:13,360
I get chatty when I drink.

179
00:13:15,279 --> 00:13:16,279
What about you?

180
00:13:17,240 --> 00:13:18,519
You blush when you drink.

181
00:13:21,759 --> 00:13:22,480
You're seeing things.

182
00:13:22,559 --> 00:13:23,600
When you're drunk,

183
00:13:24,519 --> 00:13:25,799
the things you say

184
00:13:26,360 --> 00:13:27,759
might actually be true.

185
00:13:28,200 --> 00:13:29,200
Let go.

186
00:13:30,200 --> 00:13:31,600
I won't.

187
00:13:33,240 --> 00:13:35,559
Everything we missed over the years,

188
00:13:36,519 --> 00:13:37,759
I'm going to make up for it.

189
00:13:49,320 --> 00:13:50,320
You're drunk.

190
00:13:52,399 --> 00:13:53,440
Let's just drink.

191
00:13:54,120 --> 00:13:55,279
Once you sober up,

192
00:13:56,519 --> 00:13:57,840
we can talk business.

193
00:16:15,039 --> 00:16:16,080
0516.

194
00:16:16,440 --> 00:16:17,759
The day we met.

195
00:16:26,440 --> 00:16:27,519
What are you looking for?

196
00:16:30,200 --> 00:16:31,320
Why so tense?

197
00:16:32,000 --> 00:16:33,000
I'm just curious.

198
00:16:33,759 --> 00:16:35,639
There's nothing here you want.

199
00:16:42,320 --> 00:16:43,559
Since you're sober now,

200
00:16:44,120 --> 00:16:45,120
let's talk business.

201
00:16:46,399 --> 00:16:47,600
Hand over the route,

202
00:16:48,000 --> 00:16:49,080
and I'll spare your life.

203
00:16:49,679 --> 00:16:50,519
Spare?

204
00:16:50,679 --> 00:16:52,039
You've said that before.

205
00:16:52,559 --> 00:16:53,639
But you know

206
00:16:54,000 --> 00:16:55,320
what I want

207
00:16:55,679 --> 00:16:56,960
is more than just that.

208
00:16:59,080 --> 00:17:00,159
What do you want?

209
00:17:13,559 --> 00:17:14,759
To stay.

210
00:17:15,319 --> 00:17:16,559
You be my boss,

211
00:17:17,519 --> 00:17:18,519
and I'll

212
00:17:19,720 --> 00:17:20,720
be your man.

213
00:17:32,599 --> 00:17:33,599
Keep quiet.

214
00:17:36,880 --> 00:17:38,319
You'd better not play any tricks.

215
00:17:38,640 --> 00:17:40,039
I said I'd be your man.

216
00:17:40,519 --> 00:17:42,200
Why would I play tricks on you?

217
00:17:42,319 --> 00:17:43,279
Now

218
00:17:43,319 --> 00:17:44,759
is a great chance for you to escape.

219
00:17:44,839 --> 00:17:45,880
Lin Yan,

220
00:17:46,519 --> 00:17:47,839
do I look like that kind of guy?

221
00:18:09,039 --> 00:18:10,039
Follow me.

222
00:18:22,759 --> 00:18:23,759
Catch.

223
00:18:55,960 --> 00:18:56,960
Do you know them?

224
00:18:57,319 --> 00:18:58,319
No.

225
00:18:58,680 --> 00:18:59,839
But judging by their gear,

226
00:19:00,200 --> 00:19:01,439
they should be Nightwalkers.

227
00:19:01,440 --> 00:19:02,518
That's the highest-paid

228
00:19:02,519 --> 00:19:03,519
assassin syndicate.

229
00:19:03,599 --> 00:19:04,679
Who did you cross

230
00:19:04,680 --> 00:19:05,735
to want you dead this badly?

231
00:19:05,759 --> 00:19:07,240
He just slapped me,

232
00:19:07,599 --> 00:19:09,000
so I crippled one of his arms.

233
00:19:09,720 --> 00:19:11,199
Can't believe he'd spend thirty million

234
00:19:11,200 --> 00:19:12,280
to put a bounty on my head.

235
00:19:12,640 --> 00:19:13,640
Looks like your place

236
00:19:14,200 --> 00:19:15,480
isn't as safe as you claimed.

237
00:19:16,680 --> 00:19:18,240
I'm in the arms business.

238
00:19:18,359 --> 00:19:20,119
Moving guns and ammo in and out,

239
00:19:20,559 --> 00:19:21,640
you never know when

240
00:19:22,799 --> 00:19:24,359
a bullet might end up in your own head.

241
00:19:24,519 --> 00:19:25,759
There are way too many people

242
00:19:25,960 --> 00:19:27,200
keeping an eye on you.

243
00:19:29,200 --> 00:19:30,279
Does that include you?

244
00:19:36,759 --> 00:19:38,240
I'm the one protecting you.

245
00:19:38,920 --> 00:19:40,400
See? I'm useful, right?

246
00:19:43,039 --> 00:19:44,039
If you don't trust me,

247
00:19:44,680 --> 00:19:45,240
then why did you

248
00:19:45,241 --> 00:19:46,561
dare to give me the gun just now?

249
00:19:46,599 --> 00:19:47,640
Weren't you afraid

250
00:19:48,000 --> 00:19:49,359
I'd take the chance to kill you?

251
00:19:54,960 --> 00:19:56,200
You've already silently agreed.

252
00:19:57,640 --> 00:19:58,759
Then you can stay.

253
00:19:59,799 --> 00:20:01,799
Rather than dying by
someone else's hands one day,

254
00:20:02,160 --> 00:20:03,160
I might as well

255
00:20:04,039 --> 00:20:05,440
give this life back to you.

256
00:20:06,680 --> 00:20:08,599
Too bad you miscalculated this time.

257
00:20:08,799 --> 00:20:10,279
You didn't give your life back to me,

258
00:20:10,519 --> 00:20:11,798
but ended up owing me another one.

259
00:20:11,799 --> 00:20:13,400
I don't have time for your nonsense.

260
00:20:14,240 --> 00:20:16,080
The fact that these
people broke into my house

261
00:20:16,440 --> 00:20:17,359
means there are some things

262
00:20:17,360 --> 00:20:18,440
I have to deal with.

263
00:20:20,240 --> 00:20:21,599
I'll be waiting for you at home.

264
00:20:22,920 --> 00:20:23,920
Boss.

265
00:20:40,519 --> 00:20:41,640
A little bigger.

266
00:20:41,880 --> 00:20:42,880
Slow down, slow down.

267
00:20:44,640 --> 00:20:45,839
Get up, get up.

268
00:20:45,960 --> 00:20:46,960
Get up.

269
00:20:47,400 --> 00:20:48,400
Get up.

270
00:20:50,400 --> 00:20:51,960
Come on, be careful.

271
00:20:52,519 --> 00:20:53,519
Be careful.

272
00:20:54,240 --> 00:20:55,240
Second Uncle.

273
00:20:56,240 --> 00:20:58,078
A-ren, take the kids inside.

274
00:20:58,079 --> 00:20:59,079
Come on, follow me.

275
00:21:04,000 --> 00:21:05,000
A-yan.

276
00:21:05,359 --> 00:21:07,079
I heard something happened at your place.

277
00:21:07,279 --> 00:21:08,480
I was worried sick.

278
00:21:09,319 --> 00:21:10,440
But looking at it now,

279
00:21:11,039 --> 00:21:12,440
it doesn't seem like a big deal.

280
00:21:12,640 --> 00:21:13,640
Thanks to Nie Chuan.

281
00:21:13,759 --> 00:21:15,359
He spotted the assassins sneaking in

282
00:21:15,599 --> 00:21:16,599
and saved my life.

283
00:21:18,000 --> 00:21:20,240
The guide?

284
00:21:21,079 --> 00:21:21,640
Yes.

285
00:21:21,960 --> 00:21:23,000
He's the one who saved me.

286
00:21:23,559 --> 00:21:24,799
You trust him a lot.

287
00:21:25,200 --> 00:21:26,400
I only trust the facts.

288
00:21:29,319 --> 00:21:31,095
There's a shipment coming
up in the next couple of days.

289
00:21:31,119 --> 00:21:32,119
You handle it.

290
00:21:32,160 --> 00:21:33,640
Have him go with you.

291
00:21:39,160 --> 00:21:40,160
Got it, Second Uncle.

